# Component System

This rule defines the component system structure and standards.

## Component Categories
- **Core Components**: Essential building blocks (Button, Input, etc.)
- **Composite Components**: Complex components built from core components
- **Layout Components**: Structure and organization components
- **Page Components**: Full page templates and layouts

## Component Status System
Components can have the following statuses:
- **Draft**: In development, not ready for production
- **Ready**: Tested and approved for production use
- **Deprecated**: Scheduled for removal, use alternatives
- **Experimental**: New features being tested

## Component Structure
Each component should have:
- TypeScript definition
- Props documentation
- Usage examples
- Accessibility notes
- Theme variants
- Test coverage

## Component Browser Features
- Filter by status
- Search functionality
- Category grouping
- Interactive previews
- Code snippets
- Props table
- Theme preview

## Documentation Standards
- Clear usage guidelines
- Interactive examples
- Accessibility compliance
- Responsive behavior
- Theme variations
- Props API reference

## Example Components
- Button
- Alert
- Badge
- Card
- Dialog
- Navigation
- Form elements
- Typography components
